# Connections.mmd

## Purpose
An authoritative, high-level graph of which regions connect to which.

## Context
Read first:
- `GENRE.md`
- `setting/region/Regions.md`

## Instructions
Show the connections between regions at a high level as an authoritative representation of their relationship. No indicator of connection type or quantity is needed at this level, just that the connection exists (A connects to B, B connects to A and C, C connects to B, etc).

**Every group tier asserts existence only** - this diagram, and a DANGEROUS region's block-to-block diagram below it. Only the location tier carries connection type, because only locations are connected to one another: a location never connects to a region, and a location node never appears here.

This is written at 3b, before any location exists, so it is a claim rather than a reading: every edge here is a promise that some location in one region connects to some location in the other, and no cross-region location edge may exist without an edge here licensing it. Both directions are checked once 4c closes.

## Template
```mermaid
graph LR
    A["A - [Region Name]"] --- B["B - [Region Name]"]
```
